    deepExplanation: "Step 1 — Understand the problem.\n\nStep 1 — WITHOUT BUILT-IN / CORE: keep normalized words and filter incrementally.\n```ts\ninterface Suggestion {\n  label: string;\n  score: number;\n}\n\nfunction autocomplete(\n  items: readonly Suggestion[],\n  query: string,\n  limit = 5,\n): Suggestion[] {\n  const normalized = query.trim().toLowerCase();\n\n  return items\n    .filter((item) => item.label.toLowerCase().startsWith(normalized))\n    .sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score)\n    .slice(0, limit);\n}\n```\n\nStep 2 — WITH BUILT-IN / production-friendly alternative: pre-sort once and keep immutable results.\n```ts\ninterface Suggestion {\n  label: string;\n  score: number;\n}\n\nfunction buildAutocompleteIndex(\n  items: readonly Suggestion[],\n): Suggestion[] {\n  return [...items].sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score);\n}\n\nfunction queryAutocomplete(\n  index: readonly Suggestion[],\n  query: string,\n  limit = 5,\n): Suggestion[] {\n  const normalized = query.trim().toLowerCase();\n  const result: Suggestion[] = [];\n\n  for (const item of index) {\n    if (item.label.toLowerCase().startsWith(normalized)) {\n      result.push(item);\n      if (result.length === limit) break;\n    }\n  }\n\n  return result;\n}\n```\n\nStep 3 — Example:\n`[\"apple\", \"application\", \"banana\"]`, query `\"app\"` → `[\"apple\", \"application\"]`.\n\nStep 4 — Complexity:\nSimple scan O(n·L) in the worst case, where L is text length.\nA Trie is preferable for very large/high-QPS prefix workloads.\nFrontend production usually also debounces input and cancels stale requests.\n\nStep 5 — Interview takeaway:\nUse the simplest implementation that preserves correctness and keeps UI work bounded.",
